      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The original settlement grew around a famous chalybeate spring, known for its iron\u2011rich waters, which drew early settlers in 1847.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.hschamber.org/about",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "When the East Line and Red River Railroad reached the area in 1876, Hughes Springs became a key station and its population began to boom.",
